weighted_graphs=28, cuts=988

=== Sharp orthogonal-star boundary ===
Z^d with the all-half characteristic has delta*lambda_odd=sqrt(d)/2 for d=1,...,12.

=== Scope verdict ===
PROVED ALGEBRA: every rank-d lattice with an obtuse superbase satisfies
  delta*lambda_odd <= sqrt(d)/2,
and the constant is sharp on the orthogonal all-half family.
CITED CONSEQUENCE: every Euclidean lattice of dimension at most three is of this kind.
OPEN: no claim is made for a general lattice without an obtuse superbase.
GRAPHS=799
